1) Duomo di Milano (Milan Cathedral) — Landmark
- Why it’s great for families: Iconic Milanese landmark with stunning architecture. Rooftop access offers amazing views (kids often love the panorama).
- What to know: Tickets and timings vary; check for rooftop access and possible long lines.

2) Duomo Di Milano Guided Tour — Guided experience
- Why it’s great for families: A structured, kid-friendly way to learn the history of the cathedral with a guide.
- What to know: Includes insights you’d miss on a self-visit; durations vary.

3) Milano Design Tour — Design-focused tour
- Why it’s great for families: Fun, visually engaging way to explore Milan’s design districts, architecture, and creative spots.
- What to know: Good for curious kids who enjoy architecture and art.

4) Discover the Milano by Food — Food tour
- Why it’s great for families: Tastes and experiences along the way can be a hit with kids; hands-on feel of the city’s foodie culture.
- What to know: Pace and route can vary; great for a relaxed, tasty introduction to the city.

5) Taste Milano Food Experience in the centre — Food experience
- Why it’s great for families: Central Milan location with approachable food stops; keeps the day lively.
- What to know: Focuses on local flavors; check dietary options if needed.

